.SH NAME
md_BUILD \- 🏗️ Build & Publish Guide 
.PP


.PP
The build output is located in \fRbuild/net10\&.0/\fP\&.
.SH "Building Locally"
.PP
.SS "Windows (PowerShell)"
.PP
.nf
\&./Build\&.ps1
.fi
.PP
.SS "Linux / Unix (Make)"
.PP
.nf
make
.fi
.PP
.SH "Publishing to NuGet"
.PP
.SS "1\&. Pre-Publish Checklist"
Before publishing a new version, ensure the following files are updated:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB\fRCHANGELOG\&.md\fP\fP: Document the changes for the new release\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB\fRnuget/version\&.txt\fP\fP: Update with the target version string\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB\fRnuget/ReleaseNotes\&.md\fP\fP: Add the current changelog entry\&. 
.PP
.RS 4
📌 \fBNote:\fP Do not modify any lines below the \fR---\fP separator in \fRReleaseNotes\&.md\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
.SS "2\&. API Key Setup"
.IP "1." 4
Create a file named \fRAPI\&.txt\fP in the \fRnuget/\fP directory (\fRnuget/API\&.txt\fP) and paste your NuGet API key into it\&.
.IP "2." 4
\fBSecurity Warning:\fP Ensure that \fRAPI\&.txt\fP (along with your \fR\&.snk\fP files) is listed in your \fR\&.gitignore\fP\&. Your credentials and private keys must \fBunder no circumstances\fP be committed or pushed online!
.PP
.SS "3\&. Run Build & Push"
Execute the following commands in your terminal:

.PP
.PP
.nf
make 
make push API_KEY=$(cat \&./nuget/API\&.txt)
.fi
.PP
 
